#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b17ab2c0-a71e-5e7d-89c0-937a0a07f438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}+\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292525} {:answer/id #uuid "4027e753-7b1f-569d-b840-11bcfedf5934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4027e753-7b1f-569d-b840-11bcfedf5934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292526} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5efcb9-4aa5-5b02-9e9d-d93d68eb53f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59759616-b70c-500d-99c5-be22cfbb7cb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-348733" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+17x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}+17\\cdot 0]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{3}{2}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+17(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[0+0+0]-[0+\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}-\\frac{17\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
